From 5d4c533e1cf11466bb09417b0ccf9f95b6d577a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:42:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Node machine: sweeps by batches of expressions (#2524)

T, C and X take a batch's records each from a base: T types a batch's
expressions one after another in the columns, from base 0, and C and X
then take each one (node_machine_select). The wide values, call
arguments and update plans are the batch's, started by its first
expression. node_machine_run keeps one expression alone, at base 0.

The shadow's timing passes run the sweeps by batches (--batch N, 1 by
default): T over a batch, then C over it, then X. With --verify, each
taken expression's result by batches (its refusal, tape, labels and
calls) is checked against its result alone; the census test runs by
batches of three.

Part of #2524.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
